{
  "$comment": [
    "Language-neutral golden vectors for the safety-critical functions in @quran-ai/contracts.",
    "",
    "WHY THIS FILE EXISTS: these functions are gates, not conveniences. canShowLearnerFacingAiOutput",
    "is the only thing stopping unreviewed AI output reaching a learner; canUseExternalAsr is the only",
    "thing stopping audio leaving without guardian consent. They are currently implemented once, in",
    "TypeScript. Any second implementation (a Node service, a Dart client, a Python check) must agree",
    "EXACTLY, and prose in a design doc cannot enforce that. This corpus can: every runtime loads this",
    "same file and asserts the same expectations.",
    "",
    "The TypeScript suite (tests/platform-contracts.test.ts) consumes this file rather than",
    "duplicating the cases as literals, so the corpus is the source of truth and cannot silently",
    "drift from the language that happens to own the reference implementation today.",
    "",
    "ADDING CASES: add them here, not in a test file. A case added only to one language's suite is",
    "exactly the divergence this corpus is meant to prevent."
  ],
  "canShowLearnerFacingAiOutput": {
    "$comment": "Allowlist gate. Only teacher-reviewed / scholar-approved pass, AND confidence >= 0.82, AND at least one source. Every other input must return false.",
    "cases": [
      {
        "name": "approved: teacher-reviewed, high confidence, sourced",
        "input": {
          "confidence": 0.91,
          "reviewStatus": "teacher-reviewed",
          "sources": [
            {
              "id": "scholar-board",
              "title": "Scholar Board",
              "citation": "Approved tajweed note"
            }
          ]
        },
        "expected": true
      },
      {
        "name": "approved: scholar-approved also clears the gate",
        "input": {
          "confidence": 0.9,
          "reviewStatus": "scholar-approved",
          "sources": [
            {
              "id": "scholar-board",
              "title": "Scholar Board",
              "citation": "Approved tajweed note"
            }
          ]
        },
        "expected": true
      },
      {
        "name": "blocked: no sources",
        "input": {
          "confidence": 0.91,
          "reviewStatus": "teacher-reviewed",
          "sources": []
        },
        "expected": false
      },
      {
        "name": "blocked: draft status",
        "input": {
          "confidence": 0.91,
          "reviewStatus": "draft",
          "sources": [
            {
              "id": "scholar-board",
              "title": "Scholar Board",
              "citation": "Approved tajweed note"
            }
          ]
        },
        "expected": false
      },
      {
        "name": "blocked: teacher-review-required (queued, not yet reviewed)",
        "input": {
          "confidence": 0.91,
          "reviewStatus": "teacher-review-required",
          "sources": [
            {
              "id": "scholar-board",
              "title": "Scholar Board",
              "citation": "Approved tajweed note"
            }
          ]
        },
        "expected": false
      },
      {
        "name": "blocked: ai-suggested",
        "input": {
          "confidence": 0.99,
          "reviewStatus": "ai-suggested",
          "sources": [
            {
              "id": "scholar-board",
              "title": "Scholar Board",
              "citation": "Approved tajweed note"
            }
          ]
        },
        "expected": false
      },
      {
        "name": "blocked: confidence well below threshold",
        "input": {
          "confidence": 0.78,
          "reviewStatus": "teacher-reviewed",
          "sources": [
            {
              "id": "scholar-board",
              "title": "Scholar Board",
              "citation": "Approved tajweed note"
            }
          ]
        },
        "expected": false
      },
      {
        "name": "boundary: confidence exactly 0.82 passes (>= not >)",
        "input": {
          "confidence": 0.82,
          "reviewStatus": "teacher-reviewed",
          "sources": [
            {
              "id": "scholar-board",
              "title": "Scholar Board",
              "citation": "Approved tajweed note"
            }
          ]
        },
        "expected": true
      },
      {
        "name": "boundary: confidence 0.81 fails",
        "input": {
          "confidence": 0.81,
          "reviewStatus": "teacher-reviewed",
          "sources": [
            {
              "id": "scholar-board",
              "title": "Scholar Board",
              "citation": "Approved tajweed note"
            }
          ]
        },
        "expected": false
      },
      {
        "name": "FAILS CLOSED: unrecognized reviewStatus must block, never pass",
        "$comment": "THE most important case in this corpus. reviewStatus arrives from an HTTP JSON body with no server-side schema enforcement, so a typo or a future upstream status lands here as an unknown string. An allowlist returns false; a denylist of known-bad statuses would return TRUE and leak unreviewed output to a learner. A port using a language enum (Dart, Rust) may reject or coerce this value instead of evaluating it -- that port is wrong even if its own tests pass.",
        "input": {
          "confidence": 0.99,
          "reviewStatus": "under-review",
          "sources": [
            {
              "id": "scholar-board",
              "title": "Scholar Board",
              "citation": "Approved tajweed note"
            }
          ]
        },
        "expected": false
      },
      {
        "name": "FAILS CLOSED: empty-string reviewStatus",
        "input": {
          "confidence": 0.99,
          "reviewStatus": "",
          "sources": [
            {
              "id": "scholar-board",
              "title": "Scholar Board",
              "citation": "Approved tajweed note"
            }
          ]
        },
        "expected": false
      }
    ]
  },
  "mustDiscardAudio": {
    "$comment": "Retention gate. Only the literal 'discard' mode forces destruction.",
    "cases": [
      {
        "name": "discard mode destroys audio",
        "input": "discard",
        "expected": true
      },
      {
        "name": "teacher-review retains",
        "input": "teacher-review",
        "expected": false
      },
      {
        "name": "training-opt-in retains",
        "input": "training-opt-in",
        "expected": false
      }
    ]
  },
  "canUseExternalAsr": {
    "$comment": "AND gate: BOTH externalAsrProcessing AND guardianApproved must be true. All three false-combinations are pinned so a port cannot implement OR by mistake.",
    "cases": [
      {
        "name": "both flags true: permitted",
        "input": {
          "recordingConsent": true,
          "audioRetention": "discard",
          "anonymizedLearning": true,
          "externalAsrProcessing": true,
          "guardianApproved": true,
          "consentVersion": "pilot-v1"
        },
        "expected": true
      },
      {
        "name": "externalAsrProcessing false: blocked",
        "input": {
          "recordingConsent": true,
          "audioRetention": "discard",
          "anonymizedLearning": true,
          "externalAsrProcessing": false,
          "guardianApproved": true,
          "consentVersion": "pilot-v1"
        },
        "expected": false
      },
      {
        "name": "guardianApproved false: blocked",
        "input": {
          "recordingConsent": true,
          "audioRetention": "discard",
          "anonymizedLearning": true,
          "externalAsrProcessing": true,
          "guardianApproved": false,
          "consentVersion": "pilot-v1"
        },
        "expected": false
      },
      {
        "name": "both false: blocked (pins the AND, not an OR)",
        "input": {
          "recordingConsent": true,
          "audioRetention": "discard",
          "anonymizedLearning": true,
          "externalAsrProcessing": false,
          "guardianApproved": false,
          "consentVersion": "pilot-v1"
        },
        "expected": false
      }
    ]
  },
  "modelEvalPassesReleaseGate": {
    "$comment": "Release gate. Every threshold is pinned on its failing side individually, so a port cannot drop one check and still pass this corpus. NOTE: datasetVersion below names a dataset that does not exist -- see specs/kurdish-asr-evaluation/spec.md. It is retained verbatim as a STRUCTURAL fixture (the gate's arithmetic), not as evidence any model was evaluated.",
    "cases": [
      {
        "name": "all thresholds met",
        "input": {
          "modelVersion": "model-v1",
          "datasetVersion": "fatihah-juz-amma-reviewed-v1",
          "wordAlignmentF1": 0.91,
          "tajweedF1": 0.84,
          "falsePositiveRate": 0.06,
          "teacherAgreementRate": 0.92,
          "unsourcedLearnerOutputs": 0,
          "passed": true
        },
        "expected": true
      },
      {
        "name": "wordAlignmentF1 below 0.90",
        "input": {
          "modelVersion": "model-v1",
          "datasetVersion": "fatihah-juz-amma-reviewed-v1",
          "wordAlignmentF1": 0.89,
          "tajweedF1": 0.84,
          "falsePositiveRate": 0.06,
          "teacherAgreementRate": 0.92,
          "unsourcedLearnerOutputs": 0,
          "passed": true
        },
        "expected": false
      },
      {
        "name": "falsePositiveRate above 0.08",
        "input": {
          "modelVersion": "model-v1",
          "datasetVersion": "fatihah-juz-amma-reviewed-v1",
          "wordAlignmentF1": 0.91,
          "tajweedF1": 0.84,
          "falsePositiveRate": 0.081,
          "teacherAgreementRate": 0.92,
          "unsourcedLearnerOutputs": 0,
          "passed": true
        },
        "expected": false
      },
      {
        "name": "teacherAgreementRate below 0.90",
        "input": {
          "modelVersion": "model-v1",
          "datasetVersion": "fatihah-juz-amma-reviewed-v1",
          "wordAlignmentF1": 0.91,
          "tajweedF1": 0.84,
          "falsePositiveRate": 0.06,
          "teacherAgreementRate": 0.89,
          "unsourcedLearnerOutputs": 0,
          "passed": true
        },
        "expected": false
      },
      {
        "name": "any unsourced learner output is disqualifying",
        "input": {
          "modelVersion": "model-v1",
          "datasetVersion": "fatihah-juz-amma-reviewed-v1",
          "wordAlignmentF1": 0.91,
          "tajweedF1": 0.84,
          "falsePositiveRate": 0.06,
          "teacherAgreementRate": 0.92,
          "unsourcedLearnerOutputs": 1,
          "passed": true
        },
        "expected": false
      },
      {
        "name": "passed flag false overrides all metrics",
        "input": {
          "modelVersion": "model-v1",
          "datasetVersion": "fatihah-juz-amma-reviewed-v1",
          "wordAlignmentF1": 0.91,
          "tajweedF1": 0.84,
          "falsePositiveRate": 0.06,
          "teacherAgreementRate": 0.92,
          "unsourcedLearnerOutputs": 0,
          "passed": false
        },
        "expected": false
      }
    ]
  },
  "sha256Hex": {
    "$comment": "Byte-level cross-language anchor. UTF-8 is the ONLY correct byte source: Dart's String.codeUnits is UTF-16 and Java/Kotlin's default charset is platform-dependent -- both produce a different digest for the Arabic vector below while agreeing with TS on the ASCII ones. That is why an Arabic case is mandatory here, not optional.",
    "cases": [
      {
        "name": "empty string",
        "input": "",
        "expected": "e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855"
      },
      {
        "name": "ascii",
        "input": "abc",
        "expected": "ba7816bf8f01cfea414140de5dae2223b00361a396177a9cb410ff61f20015ad"
      },
      {
        "name": "arabic with diacritics (UTF-8, NOT UTF-16)",
        "input": "بِسْمِ",
        "expected": "1c562fd4a7951a03c69ed9f9a10f9423120f439d4fea482d35f3a5c6062dc006",
        "$note": "A UTF-16 byte source yields 4595330cb3470c17227f05845841b9b7c670a71870d7c53813e5a806ebc79881 for this same string -- verified, not assumed. That is why an Arabic vector is mandatory: the two ASCII cases above pass under BOTH encodings, so they cannot catch a Dart port using String.codeUnits."
      }
    ]
  },
  "isNonRecitedMark": {
    "$comment": "T1 — mushaf annotation vs recited word. inputCodepoints (not literal characters) because these marks are INVISIBLE in an editor and in a diff: a literal-character class in forced_align.py merged two ranges, deleted every Arabic letter, and passed review (PR #258). AGENTS.md makes escapes a hard boundary. A Dart/Node port builds the string from the codepoints and must agree.",
    "cases": [
      {
        "name": "U+06D6 waqf sad-lam-alef",
        "inputCodepoints": [
          1750
        ],
        "expected": true
      },
      {
        "name": "U+06D7 waqf qaf-lam-alef",
        "inputCodepoints": [
          1751
        ],
        "expected": true
      },
      {
        "name": "U+06D8 compulsory pause",
        "inputCodepoints": [
          1752
        ],
        "expected": true
      },
      {
        "name": "U+06D9 do not pause",
        "inputCodepoints": [
          1753
        ],
        "expected": true
      },
      {
        "name": "U+06DA waqf jeem",
        "inputCodepoints": [
          1754
        ],
        "expected": true
      },
      {
        "name": "U+06DB three dots",
        "inputCodepoints": [
          1755
        ],
        "expected": true
      },
      {
        "name": "U+06DC small high seen",
        "inputCodepoints": [
          1756
        ],
        "expected": true
      },
      {
        "name": "U+06DD end of ayah",
        "inputCodepoints": [
          1757
        ],
        "expected": true
      },
      {
        "name": "U+06DE start of rub el hizb",
        "inputCodepoints": [
          1758
        ],
        "expected": true
      },
      {
        "name": "U+06E9 place of sajdah",
        "inputCodepoints": [
          1769
        ],
        "expected": true
      },
      {
        "name": "real word bismi — must stay scored",
        "inputCodepoints": [
          1576,
          1616,
          1587,
          1618,
          1605,
          1616
        ],
        "expected": false
      },
      {
        "name": "word CARRYING a mark is still a word (the dangerous loose rule would drop it)",
        "inputCodepoints": [
          1576,
          1616,
          1587,
          1618,
          1605,
          1616,
          1754
        ],
        "expected": false
      },
      {
        "name": "empty string",
        "inputCodepoints": [],
        "expected": false
      },
      {
        "name": "whitespace only cannot be a mark",
        "inputCodepoints": [
          32
        ],
        "expected": false
      },
      {
        "name": "whitespace-padded mark is a mark",
        "inputCodepoints": [
          32,
          1754,
          32
        ],
        "expected": true
      },
      {
        "name": "word-internal combining mark U+06EC is not standalone annotation",
        "inputCodepoints": [
          1772
        ],
        "expected": false
      }
    ]
  }
}
